  reflected conjugate J; matrix elements of slab words are these
  correlations>|<cell|same J, R, labels>|<cell|input>>|<row|<cell|C03-to-C04-reflection-J>|<cell|C03
  (<verbatim|reflection.tex> l.13\U15) \<rightarrow\>
  heat-vectors>|<cell|Word pairing reflects the first tuple in time and
  applies the reflected conjugate J to its labels>|<cell|J = reflected
  conjugate on every level, compatible with
  inclusions>|<cell|input>>|<row|<cell|C14-to-C04-calibrated-actions>|<cell|C14
  (<verbatim|physical-angular-actions.tex> l.304\U315) \<rightarrow\>
  label-descent (<verbatim|input:calibrated-actions>)>|<cell|Isomorphisms
  Q_d, reference actions R_d^0, T_d^0 with boost generator \<minus\>iL^0,
  agreement on spatial rotations, R_d=Q_dR_d^0Q_d^{-1} commuting with
  inclusions, involutions J_d, J_d^0 with J_dQ_d=Q_dJ_d^0,
  J_d^0T_d^0=T_d^0J_d^0>|<cell|the same Q_d that define R_d (no fresh
  choice); same inclusions as E4>|<cell|input; C14 text states it supplies
  exactly this>>|<row|<cell|C03-C14-to-C04-involution-identity
  (<strong|new>)>|<cell|C03, C14 \<rightarrow\> boundary-detection
  (<verbatim|cor:word-motion-inputs>)>|<cell|The involution J_d of
  <verbatim|input:calibrated-actions> equals the reflected conjugate J of
  <verbatim|reflection.tex> on every level>|<cell|J = \<theta\>\<kappa\>
  (time-reflection label action composed with real structure); see the
  computation after <verbatim|cor:word-motion-inputs>: \<theta\>\<kappa\>
  commutes with K_a=-iL_a, \<kappa\> alone anticommutes>|<cell|input; Lean:
  <verbatim|YM.Boundary.starRead J h> (J = time-axis adjoint of the real
  spin), used through <verbatim|YM.Boundary.Letter.rewrites>>>|<row|<cell|C14-to-C04-null-equality>|<cell|C14
  (detector chapters) \<rightarrow\> boundary-detection>|<cell|At every
  finite level, the selected null space (labels vanishing in every
  distinct-point correlation with arbitrary exterior labels) equals the
  original null space>|<cell|same hierarchy T, same
  quotient>|<cell|input>>|<row|<cell|C03-to-C04-unique-heat>|<cell|C03
  (<verbatim|phase-selection.tex>/<verbatim|phases.tex>) \<rightarrow\>
  spectral-measure, complex-heat>|<cell|The heat-fixed subspace of H_E is
  C\<Omega\>_E>|<cell|the selected (pure) phase's H_E>|<cell|input; the Lean
  <verbatim|Next/BOUNDARY/Stage.establishing> variant explicitly omits it, so
  the endpoint's use must be matched by G01>>|<row|<cell|L1>|<cell|Williams,
  <em|Lecture notes on C*-algebras>, Thm 2.19>|<cell|continuous functional
  calculus, bounded self-adjoint case>|<cell|\V>|<cell|cited (previously
  inspected; not re-inspected in this pass)>>|<row|<cell|L2>|<cell|Melrose,
  <em|Introduction to Microlocal Analysis>, Ch. 1, Thm 1.3>|<cell|Fourier
  transform is a homeomorphism of Schwartz space, radian
  convention>|<cell|\V>|<cell|cited (previously inspected; not
  re-inspected)>>|<row|<cell|L3>|<cell|Bekka\Ude la Harpe\UValette,
  <em|Kazhdan's Property (T)>, Thm D.3.1>|<cell|SNAG
  theorem>|<cell|\V>|<cell|cited (previously inspected via indexed text; not
  re-inspected)>>>>>

